module tasks.`2026-11-19-headless-node-linux`

task HeadlessNodeLinux {
  title "Nodes phase 1: headless node on macOS and Linux; make build-node and make test-linux in dory"
  verify $ make build-node && make test-linux
  paths "crates", "Makefile", "scripts", "Cargo.toml", "Cargo.lock", "verification", "LAND.md"
  brief """
    Our stand (verbatim, `specs/philosophy.md`): Find every abstraction, dependency, framework, and layer that exists only to compensate for the complexity introduced by another layer. Question every inherited architectural decision. Don't make my software more like Linux. Make it more like DOS. Everything should be inspectable, understandable, and modifiable. Subtract before you add. Minimize concepts, not lines of code. Report what you removed.

    ## Goal
    Implement [[specs/nodes]] §1, §6 and §10.1. `bboxy450-term node` runs the existing supervisor and logic entries (`crates/bboxy450-term/src/cockpit.rs:699-763`) with no window, the way `headless.rs:107` does. It works on macOS and builds and runs on Linux.

    ## Steps
    1. **The `node` subcommand.** No window and no UI dependencies at run time. It runs seats, harness, MCP and ctl. Reuse the headless path; do not add a third startup path. If `headless` and `node` turn out to be the same thing, merge them and report what was removed.
    2. **Linux build.** Gate the macOS-only code so the node builds on `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`. The places are listed in nodes §6. Use the existing Linux backends `bboxy450-keychain-file` and `bboxy450-desktop-notifications-linux`. Ideally the node build does not depend on `bbt-render` or winit at all; report the dependency tree difference.
    3. **`make build-node`** builds the node binary for the host.
    4. **`make test-linux`** follows nodes §6 exactly:
       - `dory run --rm --cpus 2 --memory 4g`;
       - the worktree mounted read-only;
       - named volumes for the Cargo registry and the target directory;
       - a Rust image pinned by digest, matching `rust-toolchain.toml`.
       It runs the node crates' tests plus a smoke: start the node, run `ctl` status against it, and spawn one zsh seat. One run at a time; refuse if one is already running.
    5. **Real process test on macOS:** start the node, attach `ctl`, list seats, stop. Kill only exact PIDs.

    ## Coordination
    Task [[tasks/2026-11-19-ui-kit-four-platforms]] is editing `crates/bbt-render` in parallel. Avoid that crate; gate it out of the node instead. Rebase before landing.

    ## Acceptance
    - [ ] `make build-node` exits 0 on macOS, and the node runs headless.
    - [ ] `make test-linux` exits 0 in dory with 2 CPUs and 4 GB.
    - [ ] The report gives the dependency tree difference between the node and the app, and what was removed.

    ## Rules
    - Read first: [[specs/mobile]], [[d1794292861627536-remote-nodes-round-4-mobile-both-platforms]], [[epics/autonomous-nodes-and-mobile]], and the repository `AGENTS.md` and `LAND.md`.
    - Work only in your worktree and the allowed paths. Use signed commits as Boxy <bboxy450@gmail.com>. Run one build or test at a time, and only targeted tests while you iterate (CPU is shared).
    - Land through `make land` yourself when verification is green (autonomous landing is authorized). Then write the report at `reports/2026-11-19-<slug>.den` and send `task_report` with the commit SHA and each command with its real exit status.
    - Unattended only: no operator clicks or prompts, and no desktop capture.
    - Latitude: you choose internal structure, names and test layout. Stop and message the Oracle only if an invariant or spec line would have to break.


    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-19 15:05 (Vesper Greywind, seat 01M7TZN6JR4PC59P45MZ14S4Q9)
    - **Worktree (supersedes the managed checkout):** `/Users/feral/mydev/bbx-node-linux`, branch `exec/node-linux`, at your ff1ab401c. `make test-formal` and `make test-linux` (dory) are the heaviest gates: run each once, alone.
    - **Build slot.** At most 2 compiling executors run machine-wide. Your seat is started only when a slot is free; run one cargo command at a time.

    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-21 15:05 (Vesper Greywind, seat 01M7VC8EK2C7DQXBNCE9V0J0MH): resume and land
    - **State:** worktree `/Users/feral/mydev/bbx-node-linux`, branch `exec/node-linux`, one signed commit `3395ce637` "Run the existing cockpit backend as a windowless node", based on an older main. Remaining from the earlier handoff: `make test-formal` + `make test-linux` (Linux via dory; Docker volumes `bboxy450-term-linux-*` are kept for it).
    - **Rebase onto origin/main (`57cc8e4e7`+):** it conflicts in `crates/bbt-mux/Cargo.toml`, `crates/bbt-mux/src/mcp/canvas.rs` and `verification/coverage.toml` (main gained SVG/artifact canvas images and new coverage rows). Keep both sides' behaviour; do not drop main's canvas image support.
    - Then `make test-formal`, `make test-linux`, `make land`. **Never run a long command in the foreground:** start each detached (`nohup sh -c '... > target/node-handoff/<step>.log 2>&1; echo $? > target/node-handoff/<step>.exit' >/dev/null 2>&1 &`) and poll briefly. One gate machine-wide (gate-repairs may be landing; `pgrep -fl 'land-fast|ci-local'`).
    - Report with the task's own verify command in `verify_result.command`.

    ## Oracle ruling, 2026-11-21 17:50: wait for the harness pin, then land
    - The fix exists: harness `bd4893b3` "Compare the loader witness against its image key" is on harness main. Term pins it in the full-suite candidate (`1e23b5207`, tasks/2026-11-21-full-suite-last-two), which is landing now.
    - **Do not bump the harness pin yourself.** Wait (detached loop, e.g. `until git fetch -q origin && git ls-tree origin/main crates/bboxy450-harness | grep -q bd4893b3; do sleep 300; done`) until origin/main pins `bd4893b3` or a descendant, then rebase `6e73f0f88`, rerun only the failed build step, and `make land` (detached, one gate machine-wide).
    - If it has not landed by 20:00, message the Oracle once.


    ## Report from seat:01M804Y8Y50DAX21VB5D0DH1PG

    The headless node landed on main as signed commit ee65ca2b7 after the harness pin fix. The macOS and Dory process smokes ran ctl and a zsh seat with zero windows and retired both backend owners. Dory passed 172 tests and built x86-64. The rebased landing gate passed 1,286 selected tests and verified native/TLC parity across 989 models. The node drops 117 macOS desktop dependencies and consolidates CLI dispatch and file key custody. The full report records the exit statuses and the unchanged pre-pin node patch.

